# Ctrl+Break (Ctrl+Scroll Lock) while the program waits for a key: the
# keyboard driver signals the OS server, which restarts the program and
# gives up the wait; keys go on working (roadmap l4.md L8). Ctrl+Break is
# typed at once, waiting for no reader: forty ticks first, so that the
# program, which starts after every driver and init (roadmap os-server.md
# P6), waits by then.
program: keys
keys: {wait 40}{ctrl-break}a
---
rx286, test build
rx286: Ctrl+Break: the program starts again
keys: started again
key 1E 61
